  "details": "Under the \"buttons\" list, the `/input/Voice` OSC address is documented on the following page: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/osc-as-input-controller \n\nIt reads as follows:\n\n\"Toggle Voice - the action will depend on whether \"Toggle Voice\" is turned on in your Settings. If so, then changing from 0 to 1 will toggle the state of mute. If \"Toggle Voice\" is turned off, then it functions like Push-To-Mute - 1 is muted, 0 is unmuted.\"\n\nHowever, when setting my in-game microphone settings to \"Push to Talk\", I experience the opposite from what is documented. When sending values on the `/input/Voice` address, 0 mutes and 1 unmutes.\n\nA correction would be appreciated :)",
